Summary: Patch old CEF and Qt WebEngine builds that read the stack base from %gs:0x8
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover (ported here)
  Version: 25.1.1
  CW-Hacks: 16900, 18582, 19114, 21548, 22584
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/ntdll/loader.c
  Changes: only the %gs entries of CX's apply_binary_patches, in a function
    of their own; the command-line and cohtml entries are
    ntdll-cef-command-line-args and ntdll-cohtml-branch. The bounds check
    counts the patch's size, and the protection change covers the patched
    bytes rather than one page. CW HACK 22434's pe_module_loaded call, in
    the same place, is ntdll-d3dmetal-code-regions
  Note: Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: ntdll.dll (x86_64) has
    apply_binary_patches and every 'CEF %gs 85.3.11-0/1, 85.3.9.0,
    72.0.3626.121-0..2, 72.0.3626.96-0..2', 'CEF/Qt5WebEngineCore %gs
    5.15.2.0-0/1'
Upstream: differently (3a16aabb, Wine 10.5: WineHQ points GSBASE at the TEB
 while PE code runs on macOS)
Needed until: 10.5 (WineHQ 3a16aabb, Brendan Shanks)
Why: On macOS before Wine 10.5, %gs in PE code is macOS's thread data, not
 the TEB, so code that reads TEB->StackBase as %gs:0x8 gets garbage. Old
 CEF and Qt WebEngine builds do, and crash. When libcef.dll or
 Qt5WebEngineCore.dll loads and the bytes at a known offset match, those
 reads are rewritten to go through TEB->Self at %gs:0x30. Measured on
 10.0 build0: %gs:0x8 isn't the stack base there; on 11.22 it is, so this
 patch has no 11.x copy.
Programs: Rockstar Games Launcher/Social Club (CEF 85.3.9, 85.3.11),
 BeamNG.drive (CEF 72.0.3626.121), Wizard101 (CEF 72.0.3626.96), EA
 app/Origin (Qt WebEngine 5.15.2): crash at start
Matches: dll libcef.dll, Qt5WebEngineCore.dll (x86_64, exact case); bytes
 at fixed offsets: 0x28c5190, 0x28c521a (CEF 85.3.11), 0x28c4b30 (CEF
 85.3.9), 0x23bb2ad, 0x23bb329, 0x23bb369 (CEF 72.0.3626.121), 0x23bb82d,
 0x23bb8a9, 0x23bb8e9 (CEF 72.0.3626.96), 0x2810f10, 0x2810f8d (Qt
 WebEngine 5.15.2)
Seen on: macOS 26.7.2 (M1 Max): on wine-macfixes-10.0-build0, %gs:0x8
 isn't TEB->StackBase (probe program)
Fine on: macOS 26.7.2 (M1 Max): on wine-macfixes-11.22-build0, %gs:0x8 is
 TEB->StackBase (probe program)
Messages: "Found matching %s, applying patch '%s'", "%s doesn't match patch
 '%s'", "%s too small to match patch '%s'" (TRACE, channel module; only
 with +module)
Risk: always on: rewrites code in third-party DLLs, but only on an exact
 byte match at a fixed offset, so only in the builds CX tested
Uncertain: not run with any of the programs.
Expects before it: ntdll-d3dmetal-code-regions (context)
Related: ntdll-cef-command-line-args; the other libcef.dll patch at load
No test: needs specific CEF and Qt WebEngine builds
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: split out of ntdll-cef-binary-patches (review
 decision 8), with the bounds and protection fixes
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

